  "body": "The Lanes date rail printed `Aug 15` with no weekday, so telling a weekend from a weekday meant counting. It now prints `Sat Aug 15`.\n\n- date column widened 56 → 74px to fit the extra three characters (the chart lives in a horizontal scroll box, so nothing clips — checked at 390px)\n- rail label lifted from `#666666` to `#8a8a8a`; the first attempt put the weekday at 60% opacity over `#666`, which landed near `#3d3d3d` on the near-black background and was unreadable\n- hover panel gets the weekday too\n\nAlso removes the hover panel's empty state — the \"Hover a stripe for detail\" hint plus the stripe/lane counts, which were permanent furniture for a one-time instruction. The panel now renders only while a stripe is hovered: `null` on a phone, where it sits below the chart, and an equal-width spacer on desktop, where dropping the column outright would reflow the chart on every hover.\n\nVerified with headless screenshots at 390px and 1280px; weekdays cross-checked against `Date`. Lint and `npm run build` clean.",
